<title>BELGIUM: BELGIUM TO IMPOSE NEW TAX ON COMPANY CARS.</title>
<headline>BELGIUM TO IMPOSE NEW TAX ON COMPANY CARS.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian government said in its 1997 budget statement on Tuesday it would start charging social security contributions for company cars.</p>
<p>The measure was worth four billion francs, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Many Belgian companies offer employees a company a car as part of their salary package. Until now, cars were not subject to social security charges, as salaries are.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
